---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---
<Base title="Life insurance" description="Life insurance for final expenses, a mortgage or a gift to the grandkids, explained plainly by a local agent in McKees Rocks, PA.">
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Life insurance"
    title="Start with what you want the money to do."
    intro="Cover a funeral so the kids do not have to. Pay off the house. Leave something for the grandkids. Each one points to a different kind of policy."
    photo="grandparent"
  />

  <section class="section-pad" aria-labelledby="kinds-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="max-w-[42rem]" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Three common kinds</p>
        <h2 id="kinds-h" class="mt-3">The short version.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3" data-stagger role="list">
        <li class="card p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3>Final expense</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">A smaller whole life policy meant for funeral costs and last bills. Many are built for people in their 60s, 70s and older.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3>Term life</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Covers a set number of years, like the rest of a mortgage. Usually the lowest cost per dollar of coverage.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="card p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3>Whole life</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">Lasts your whole life as long as premiums are paid, and can build cash value over time.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Prose heading="Already have a policy?" eyebrow="A second look" tone="sage">
    <p>Bring it. Many people bought coverage decades ago through work or a salesman at the door and are not sure what it does now.</p>
    <p>I will read through it with you and tell you what it covers in plain words. If it still does the job, keep it.</p>
  </Prose>

  <Prose heading="What to expect." eyebrow="How I help">
    <ul>
      <li>A short talk about who you want to protect, and how much.</li>
      <li>Some policies ask health questions. Some do not. I explain the tradeoff.</li>
      <li>Prices from the companies I carry, side by side. No pressure to pick one that day.</li>
    </ul>
  </Prose>
</Base>
